# Training exam: 24 tasks, each with mechanical checks and a reference solution.
# Tools: chronos, krypton, calliope, iridium, hades, sphinx. Offline, under 10 seconds each.

== t01-chronos-retag
prompt: The tag old-build points at a commit that was never meant to ship. Delete that tag, then tag the newest commit as ok-build.
setup: run chronos init
setup: write app/main.txt
| version one
setup: run chronos add app/main.txt
setup: run chronos commit -m "first"
setup: run chronos tag old-build
setup: write app/main.txt
| version two
setup: run chronos add app/main.txt
setup: run chronos commit -m "second"
check: chronos tag => contains ok-build
check: chronos tag => lacks old-build
solution: run chronos tag -d old-build
solution: run chronos tag ok-build
solution: done Deleted old-build and tagged the newest commit as ok-build.

== t02-hades-sort-into-folders
prompt: The disk image disk.img has four files in /inbox. Move a.txt and c.txt into a new folder /keep, leaving b.txt and d.txt in /inbox. Then tell me how many files remain in /inbox.
setup: run hades --json mkfs disk.img --blocks 256
setup: run hades --json mkdir disk.img /inbox
setup: write data/a.txt
| alpha text
setup: write data/b.txt
| beta text
setup: write data/c.txt
| gamma text
setup: write data/d.txt
| delta text
setup: run hades --json put disk.img data/a.txt /inbox/a.txt
setup: run hades --json put disk.img data/b.txt /inbox/b.txt
setup: run hades --json put disk.img data/c.txt /inbox/c.txt
setup: run hades --json put disk.img data/d.txt /inbox/d.txt
check: hades --json ls disk.img /keep => contains c.txt
check: hades --json ls disk.img /inbox => lacks a.txt
check: answer => contains 2
solution: run hades --json mkdir disk.img /keep
solution: run hades --json cat disk.img /inbox/a.txt --out a.txt
solution: run hades --json put disk.img a.txt /keep/a.txt
solution: run hades --json rm disk.img /inbox/a.txt
solution: run hades --json cat disk.img /inbox/c.txt --out c.txt
solution: run hades --json put disk.img c.txt /keep/c.txt
solution: run hades --json rm disk.img /inbox/c.txt
solution: done 2 files remain in /inbox.

== t03-iridium-flag-large-open
prompt: In inv.idb, flag every invoice that is still open and larger than 100 by setting its status to review. Then tell me the total amount of all invoices now marked review.
setup: run iridium --json sql inv.idb "CREATE TABLE invoices (id INTEGER, customer TEXT, amount INTEGER, status TEXT)"
setup: run iridium --json sql inv.idb "INSERT INTO invoices VALUES (1, 'Kiran', 250, 'open'), (2, 'Ravi', 80, 'open'), (3, 'Mona', 1200, 'open'), (4, 'Yusuf', 500, 'paid'), (5, 'Tej', 340, 'open'), (6, 'Nia', 60, 'paid')"
check: iridium sql inv.idb "SELECT customer FROM invoices WHERE status = 'review' ORDER BY id" => contains Mona
check: iridium sql inv.idb "SELECT customer FROM invoices WHERE status = 'open' ORDER BY id" => lacks Mona
check: answer => contains 1790
solution: run iridium sql inv.idb "UPDATE invoices SET status = 'review' WHERE status = 'open' AND amount > 100"
solution: run iridium sql inv.idb "SELECT SUM(amount) AS total FROM invoices WHERE status = 'review'"
solution: done 1790

== t04-krypton-settings-gate
prompt: Write a shell script named deploy-check.sh. It must exit with status 0 when the file settings.ini exists in the current folder, and exit with status 4 when it does not. Then create settings.ini containing the single line mode=fast, and run the script.
check: krypton deploy-check.sh => exit 0
check: read settings.ini => contains mode=fast
check: read deploy-check.sh => contains settings.ini
solution: write deploy-check.sh
| if [ -f settings.ini ]; then
| exit 0
| fi
| exit 4
solution: write settings.ini
| mode=fast
solution: run krypton deploy-check.sh
solution: done The script exits 0 because settings.ini exists.

== t05-calliope-todo-lines
prompt: todo.txt is a list of errands. Find every line that starts with TODO, write their line numbers separated by single spaces into todo-lines.txt, and tell me the highest of those line numbers.
setup: write todo.txt
| errands for monday
| TODO fix sink
| buy bread
| walk dog
| call mum
| water plants
| TODO renew passport
| read book
| clean car
| pay bills
| TODO book dentist
| sleep early
check: read todo-lines.txt => contains 2 7 11
check: answer => contains 11
solution: run calliope --json grep "^TODO" todo.txt
solution: write todo-lines.txt
| 2 7 11
solution: done 11

== t06-calliope-add-header
prompt: header.txt is missing its first line. Add the line "# generated by tool" as the new first line, and keep the two existing lines unchanged.
setup: write header.txt
| name = relay
| port = 7001
check: read header.txt => contains # generated by tool
check: calliope --json grep "^# generated" header.txt => contains generated
solution: write fix.edit
| goto 1 1
| insert # generated by tool
| newline
| save
solution: run calliope --json edit fix.edit header.txt
solution: done Added the generated line at the top.

