== t08-chronos-untrack-secret
prompt: secrets.txt was committed by mistake. Stop tracking it in the repository but keep the file on disk, and record that as a commit with the message untrack secrets.
setup: run chronos init
setup: write secrets.txt
| api key 99-zed
setup: write app.txt
| app code
setup: run chronos add -A
setup: run chronos commit -m "initial"
check: chronos log => contains untrack secrets
check: read secrets.txt => contains api key 99-zed
check: chronos status => contains secrets.txt
solution: run chronos rm --cached secrets.txt
solution: run chronos commit -m "untrack secrets"
solution: done Stopped tracking secrets.txt and committed the change.

== t09-hades-sum-report
prompt: The disk image store.img holds /reports/q3.txt, a list of regional sales lines. Read that file from the image, add up the amounts on its lines, write the total as the only line of total.txt, and tell me the total.
setup: run hades --json mkfs store.img --blocks 256
setup: run hades --json mkdir store.img /reports
setup: write data/q3.txt
| north 4411
| south 2290
| west 1208
setup: run hades --json put store.img data/q3.txt /reports/q3.txt
check: read total.txt => contains 7909
check: answer => contains 7909
solution: run hades --json cat store.img /reports/q3.txt
solution: write total.txt
| 7909
solution: done 7909

== t10-krypton-make-notes
prompt: Write a shell script named make-notes.sh. For each argument it receives, it must create a file named NAME.txt, where NAME is that argument, containing the line note for NAME. Run the script with the arguments alpha and beta.
check: read alpha.txt => contains note for alpha
check: read beta.txt => contains note for beta
check: read beta.txt => lacks note for alpha
solution: write make-notes.sh
| for n in "$@"; do
| echo "note for $n" > "$n.txt"
| done
solution: run krypton make-notes.sh alpha beta
solution: done Created alpha.txt and beta.txt.

== t11-iridium-engineering-raise
prompt: In staff.idb, give every Engineering employee a raise of 2500 on their salary. Then tell me the total Engineering payroll after the raise.
setup: run iridium --json sql staff.idb "CREATE TABLE staff (name TEXT, dept TEXT, salary INTEGER)"
setup: run iridium --json sql staff.idb "INSERT INTO staff VALUES ('Ana', 'Engineering', 60000), ('Ben', 'Engineering', 40000), ('Cam', 'Operations', 50000), ('Dee', 'Engineering', 80000)"
check: iridium sql staff.idb "SELECT salary FROM staff WHERE name = 'Dee'" => contains 82500
check: answer => contains 187500
solution: run iridium sql staff.idb "UPDATE staff SET salary = salary + 2500 WHERE dept = 'Engineering'"
solution: run iridium sql staff.idb "SELECT SUM(salary) AS payroll FROM staff WHERE dept = 'Engineering'"
solution: done 187500

