== t21-chronos-stash-spike
prompt: You are on main with unfinished edits in draft.txt. Put those edits aside, add one commit with the message spike start on the existing branch spike that creates spike.txt containing the line spike ok, go back to main, bring the unfinished edits back, and commit draft.txt on main with the message finish draft.
setup: run chronos init
setup: write draft.txt
| draft v1
setup: run chronos add draft.txt
setup: run chronos commit -m "base"
setup: run chronos branch spike
setup: write draft.txt
| unfinished line
check: chronos log => contains finish draft
check: read draft.txt => contains unfinished line
check: chronos status => lacks draft.txt
solution: run chronos stash push
solution: run chronos switch spike
solution: write spike.txt
| spike ok
solution: run chronos add spike.txt
solution: run chronos commit -m "spike start"
solution: run chronos switch main
solution: run chronos stash pop
solution: run chronos add draft.txt
solution: run chronos commit -m "finish draft"
solution: done Committed the unfinished edits on main as finish draft.

== t22-sphinx-hmac-record
