setup: write msg.txt
| pay 40 to ada
check: read mac.txt => contains eb270940a8208126519ecf91d02a73974df149f04244bf22acb4a17ef9011177
check: answer => contains eb270940a8208126519ecf91d02a73974df149f04244bf22acb4a17ef9011177
solution: run sphinx --json hmac 4a656665 msg.txt
solution: write mac.txt
| eb270940a8208126519ecf91d02a73974df149f04244bf22acb4a17ef9011177
solution: read mac.txt
solution: done eb270940a8208126519ecf91d02a73974df149f04244bf22acb4a17ef9011177

== t23-krypton-fill-squares
prompt: Create a table named squares in nums.idb with an integer id column and an integer sq column. Write a shell script named fill.sh that, given a number N as its argument, inserts one row for each id from 1 to N, where sq holds id times id. Run it with N set to 12, then check that the table has 12 rows, and tell me the sum of the sq column.
check: iridium sql nums.idb "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM squares" => contains 12
check: iridium sql nums.idb "SELECT sq FROM squares WHERE id = 12" => contains 144
check: answer => contains 650
solution: run iridium --json sql nums.idb "CREATE TABLE squares (id INTEGER, sq INTEGER)"
solution: write fill.sh
| i=1
| while [ $i -le $1 ]; do
| iridium --json sql nums.idb "INSERT INTO squares VALUES ($i, $((i * i)))"
| i=$((i + 1))
| done
solution: read fill.sh
solution: run krypton fill.sh 12
solution: run iridium sql nums.idb "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM squares"
solution: run iridium sql nums.idb "SELECT SUM(sq) AS total FROM squares"
solution: done 650

== t24-krypton-biggest-argument
prompt: Write a shell script named biggest.sh that prints the largest of the whole numbers given as its arguments. Run it with the arguments 17 4 23 9 8 and tell me what it printed.
check: krypton biggest.sh 17 4 23 9 8 => contains 23
check: krypton biggest.sh 3 30 11 => contains 30
check: answer => contains 23
solution: write biggest.sh
| big=0
| for n in "$@"; do
| if [ "$n" -gt "$big" ]; then big=$n; fi
| done
| echo $big
solution: read biggest.sh
solution: run krypton biggest.sh 17 4 23 9 8
solution: done 23
